1.39.m:
Jayadhvaja said:
Listen, O tiger among Brahmins, to what was done formerly by me;
because I remember my past lives, I know that which produces wonder in the hearers.

1.40.m:
Nevertheless, all the gods, longing for birth in Bhārata,
worship the lord of gods, the flawless Nārāyaṇa;
the multitudes of deities headed by Brahmā constantly revere them.
